/-! # The Riemann Hypothesis, as an actual file

The compact edition (grh-compact, lsernau/grh-lean @ 72fead102f663d5c7a407964a13dc0cf9d977207),
all 794 modules, concatenated in import order into one Lean file with real line breaks. Build it in any
Lake project pinned to Lean 4.35.0 and Mathlib 56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679:
`lake env lean --tstack=400000 ManyLineRH.lean`.

The proof is by Levent Alpöge with Claude; the compact rewrite is by Luke Sernau and colleagues at
Anthropic with Claude. Apache-2.0: see LICENSE, NOTICE and ATTRIBUTION.md (whose `src/...` paths
are the `-- ═══ src/... ═══` markers below).

Each module is wrapped in its own `section`, so its `open`s, `variable`s, `set_option`s and local
attributes stay local. In one file every module also sees every earlier module, not only its
imports, so a few things were adjusted. No theorem statement or proof idea changed:
* 23 global `attribute [simp]`/`[instance]` lines that tag declarations from other files became
  `attribute [local ...]`. They stay in force to the end of their own file. They are replayed only
  in the modules that import them, on the lines ending in `-- from <module>`.
* Instances and `@[simp]` lemmas are switched off in the later modules that do not import them
  but could see them, because the statement only uses Mathlib and declarations those modules
  do import. These are the `-- single-file: ... not imported here` lines.
  So that they can be named there, 101 unnamed instances got their original auto-generated names,
  and 3 `deriving instance` lines are written out as named instances. A few further instances from
  RegularRepL2 and BaseChangePlaces are switched off the same way.
* Lean reuses auxiliary proofs and `match` helpers within one file. Each module starts with
  fresh caches (`RHSingleFile.freshCaches`), so its terms elaborate exactly as they did in its own file.
* Kronecker's `scoped[Kronecker]` simp set is renamed `scoped[RHKronecker]`. Mathlib's own
  `Kronecker` namespace would otherwise carry it everywhere. Modules that open Kronecker also
  `open scoped RHKronecker`. The scoped attributes of `PolyRep` (BranchingVector), `Filling` (Setup)
  and `Lift` (CokernelKillers) are renamed the same way (`RHPolyRep`, `RHFilling`, `RHLift`), because
  other files open those namespaces without importing them. Modules that do import them get
  `open scoped RH...` wherever they open or enter the namespace.
* 5 names were qualified where another file's declaration made them ambiguous: `PeriodPair.G`
  (CurveTheta), `PiLp.norm_apply_le` (MassBasic), `Sum.inl` (BigCell), `Lift.Pairing.IsSafe` (LongGap)
  and `_root_.loss` (OnePlaceDefect).

The companion file RestsOnRH.lean imports this one and runs `restsOn` from
google-deepmind/formal-conjectures PR #8340 on the five main theorems. -/

open Lean Meta Match in
open private matcherExt from Lean.Meta.Match.Match in
/-- Lean shares auxiliary proofs and `match` helpers inside one file. Each original module starts
with fresh caches here, as it would as a separate file, so terms elaborate exactly as before. -/
def RHSingleFile.freshCaches : CoreM Unit :=
  modifyEnv fun env => matcherExt.modifyState (auxLemmasExt.modifyState env fun _ => {}) fun _ => {}

